"Dominion (1867 カナダ、1907 の植民地会議で呼び名を統一)、responsible government (責任政府)、「帝国内の自治的共同体」(1926 バルフォア報告)、Commonwealth": "Dominion (Canada 1867; the name standardized at the 1907 Colonial Conference), responsible government, “autonomous communities within the British Empire” (Balfour Report 1926), Commonwealth",
"1931 年のウェストミンスター憲章の後の形。法では外交・軍事・課税は自前、枢密院司法委員会への上訴は残り (カナダは 1949 年、オーストラリアは 1986 年まで)、総督は国王が任命し、王位の継承は共通 (1936 年の退位では各自治領の同意が要った)。それより前 (1867〜1926) は外交を英が握り (ICOW はカナダを 1867 年に独立としつつ、外交を英が握ったとして COW の国家には 1920 年から入れる)、1914 年の宣戦は自動だった。1926 年のバルフォア報告「地位は平等で、内外のどの面でも互いに従属しない」が法になったのが 1931 年": "The form after the Statute of Westminster 1931. De jure, foreign affairs, the military and taxation were their own; appeals to the Judicial Committee of the Privy Council remained (until 1949 for Canada, 1986 for Australia); the governor-general was appointed by the King, and succession to the throne was shared (the 1936 abdication required each Dominion’s consent). Before that (1867–1926) Britain held foreign affairs (ICOW treats Canada as independent from 1867, while noting that Britain held its foreign affairs; COW counts it as a state only from 1920), and the 1914 declaration of war applied automatically. The 1926 Balfour Report’s “equal in status, in no way subordinate one to another in any aspect of their domestic or external affairs” became law in 1931",
"British North America Act 1867、1926 年帝国会議の帝国間関係委員会報告 (バルフォア報告。Cmd. 2768)、ウェストミンスター憲章 (1931 年 12 月 11 日。22 Geo. 5 c. 4。第 2 条 植民地法有効法の不適用、第 4 条 要請と同意のない英の法は及ばない、前文 王位継承法の変更には全自治領の同意)、1930 年帝国会議の総督の任命の決まり、Hancock『Survey of British Commonwealth Affairs』(1937〜42)。文書館: TNA CO 886 (Dominions)、DO シリーズ": "British North America Act 1867; report of the Inter-Imperial Relations Committee of the 1926 Imperial Conference (Balfour Report, Cmd. 2768); Statute of Westminster (December 11, 1931; 22 Geo. 5 c. 4; s. 2 non-application of the Colonial Laws Validity Act, s. 4 no British act extends to a Dominion without its request and consent, preamble: changes to the law of succession require the consent of all Dominions); the 1930 Imperial Conference rules on appointing governors-general; Hancock, Survey of British Commonwealth Affairs (1937–42). Archives: TNA CO 886 (Dominions), DO series",
"Darwin 1999「A Third British Empire?」(OHBE 第 4 巻: 自治領は帝国の弱まりか作り直しか)、Mansergh 1969『The Commonwealth Experience』、Belich 2009『Replenishing the Earth』(入植者の植民地は別の型)。論点: 自治領は「独立国」か、いつ独立したのか (1867・1926・1931・1949 で説が分かれ、データセットの入れ方も分かれる)": "Darwin 1999, “A Third British Empire?” (OHBE vol. 4: were the Dominions a weakening or a remaking of the empire), Mansergh 1969, The Commonwealth Experience, Belich 2009, Replenishing the Earth (settler colonies as a distinct type). Issues: were the Dominions “independent states”, and when did they become independent (views split among 1867, 1926, 1931 and 1949, and so do the datasets’ codings)",
"責任政府から自治領までの長い道筋 (1848〜1931) を 1 つの型にする。王冠への共通の忠誠は忠誠度の数で代える": "Folds the long path from responsible government to Dominion (1848–1931) into 1 type. Shared allegiance to the Crown is represented by the loyalty value",
