"蒙古聯合自治政府 (蒙疆)": "Mongolian United Autonomous Government (Mengjiang)",
"汪兆銘政権 (南京国民政府)": "Wang Jingwei regime (Reorganized National Government, Nanjing)",
"puppet state (リットン報告 1932 の言葉は「日本の官吏と顧問が実権を握る」)、満洲国側の言葉は「独立国」「王道楽土」「日満一徳一心」": "puppet state (the Lytton Report, 1932: “Japanese officials and advisers hold real power”); Manchukuo's own terms: “independent state”, “paradise of the Kingly Way”, “Japan and Manchukuo, one virtue and one heart”",
"法と実態の差そのものが型。法では独立国で、条約を結び (日満議定書 1932 年 9 月 15 日: 前文で日本が満洲国の独立の「事実を確認」し、満洲国は日本の既得権益を確認し、共同防衛のため日本軍の駐屯を認める)、執政 → 皇帝 (溥儀) を持つ。実態は関東軍と総務庁 (日本人の次長) が決め、人事・経済 (満鉄・日満経済ブロック)・治外法権 (1937 年に撤廃) を日本が握った。承認した国は少数 (エルサルバドル・バチカン (事実上)・独伊など)。1945 年に消滅": "The de jure–de facto gap is itself the type. De jure an independent state that concluded treaties (Japan–Manchukuo Protocol, September 15, 1932: in the preamble Japan “confirms the fact” of Manchukuo's independence, Manchukuo confirms Japan's existing rights and interests and permits Japanese troops to be stationed for joint defense) and had a Chief Executive, later Emperor (Puyi). De facto, the Kwantung Army and the General Affairs Agency (with a Japanese deputy director) decided, and Japan held appointments, the economy (the South Manchuria Railway, the Japan–Manchukuo economic bloc) and extraterritoriality (abolished in 1937). Few states recognized it (El Salvador, the Vatican (de facto), Germany, Italy and others). Dissolved in 1945",
"日満議定書 (1932 年 9 月 15 日。本文と付属の秘密協定)、リットン報告書 (国際連盟、1932 年 10 月 1 日。第 6 章)、満洲国組織法 (1932)、日満の治外法権撤廃条約 (1937 年 11 月 5 日)、外務省外交史料館・防衛研究所の関東軍の文書、アジア歴史資料センター (JACAR) でデジタル化済み": "Japan–Manchukuo Protocol (September 15, 1932; main text and attached secret agreements), Lytton Report (League of Nations, October 1, 1932; Chapter 6), Organic Law of Manchukuo (1932), Japan–Manchukuo treaty abolishing extraterritoriality (November 5, 1937), Kwantung Army records at the Diplomatic Archives of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the National Institute for Defense Studies, digitized by the Japan Center for Asian Historical Records (JACAR)",
"Duara 2003『Sovereignty and Authenticity』(「傀儡」で片付けず、満洲国を近代の主権の形として読む)、山室信一 1993『キメラ』、Mitter 2000、Yamamuro 英訳 2006。論点: 傀儡と衛星国と保護国の境、現地の協力者 (満洲国の中国人の官僚) をどう見るか": "Duara 2003, “Sovereignty and Authenticity” (reads Manchukuo as a modern form of sovereignty rather than dismissing it as a “puppet”); Yamamuro Shin'ichi 1993, “Kimera” (Chimera); Mitter 2000; Yamamuro, English translation 2006. Debates: where puppet, satellite and protectorate meet; how to view local collaborators (Manchukuo's Chinese officials)",
"承認の多さ (国際的な正統性) を数にしない。現地の協力者の層は、レーン D の集団が入るまで 1 つの行為者にする": "Breadth of recognition (international legitimacy) is not counted. The layer of local collaborators is a single actor until the Lane D groups arrive",
