"buffer state、「英国の助言と希望に従って外交を行う」(ガンダマク 1879)、補助金 (subsidy)、勢力圏 (sphere of influence)。アフガニスタン側の言葉は「アミールの独立」": "buffer state, “conduct foreign relations in accordance with the advice and wishes of the British Government” (Gandamak 1879), subsidy, sphere of influence. The Afghan term: “the Amir's independence”",
"2 つの大国の間で、片方が外交だけを握り、内政・軍事・課税・法は自前。ガンダマク条約 (1879 年 5 月 26 日) でアフガニスタンの外交は英の助言に従い、英は補助金 (デュアランド協定 1893: 年 180 万ルピー) を払った。1907 年の英露協商でロシアはアフガニスタンを英の勢力圏と認め、英は併合しないと約束した。英はアミールの継承に関わり (1880 年のアブドゥッラフマーンの承認)、1919 年のラーワルピンディー条約で外交が戻った。ネパール (スガウリ 1816) とシャム (英仏宣言 1896) も外交の制限と領土の保障の形": "Between two great powers, one holds only foreign affairs; domestic affairs, military, taxation and law remain the state's own. Under the Treaty of Gandamak (May 26, 1879), Afghan foreign relations followed British advice, and Britain paid a subsidy (Durand Agreement 1893: 1.8 million rupees a year). In the Anglo-Russian Convention of 1907 Russia recognized Afghanistan as within the British sphere, and Britain promised not to annex it. Britain had a hand in the Amir's succession (recognition of Abdur Rahman in 1880), and the Treaty of Rawalpindi in 1919 restored foreign affairs. Nepal (Sugauli 1816) and Siam (Anglo-French Declaration 1896) also took the form of restricted foreign affairs and guaranteed territory",
"ガンダマク条約 (1879 年 5 月 26 日。第 3 条 外交は英の助言に従う、第 4 条 カブールの英の代表、第 11 条 補助金)、デュアランド協定 (1893 年 11 月 12 日)、英露協商 (1907 年 8 月 31 日。アフガニスタンに関する協定第 1 条: 英は政治上の地位を変えず、露は勢力圏の外と認めて関係は英を通す)、ラーワルピンディー条約 (1919 年 8 月 8 日)、スガウリ条約 (1816 年 3 月 4 日)、英ネパール条約 (1923 年 12 月 21 日)、英仏宣言 (1896 年 1 月 15 日)。文書館: British Library IOR L/PS (政治・秘密部)": "Treaty of Gandamak (May 26, 1879; Article 3: foreign relations follow British advice; Article 4: British representative at Kabul; Article 11: subsidy), Durand Agreement (November 12, 1893), Anglo-Russian Convention (August 31, 1907; Article 1 of the agreement on Afghanistan: Britain will not change its political status; Russia recognizes it as outside its sphere and conducts relations through Britain), Treaty of Rawalpindi (August 8, 1919), Treaty of Sugauli (March 4, 1816), Anglo-Nepalese Treaty (December 21, 1923), Anglo-French Declaration (January 15, 1896). Archives: British Library IOR L/PS (Political and Secret Department)",
"Fazal 2007『State Death』(緩衝国は消滅しやすい、1816〜2000 の数で)、Partem 1983 (JCR 27-1)、Yapp 1980。論点: 緩衝国は型か位置か (地理の条件が型を決める例)、補助金は従属か取引か": "Fazal 2007, “State Death” (buffer states are prone to dying, counted over 1816–2000); Partem 1983 (JCR 27-1); Yapp 1980. Debates: is a buffer state a type or a position (a case of geography deciding the type); is a subsidy dependency or a bargain",
"2 つの大国の間という地理の条件は、H3 で AI の型の決め方 (力の差と位置) に入れる。補助金の額の交渉": "The geographic condition of lying between two great powers goes into the AI's choice of type in H3 (power gap and position). Negotiation of subsidy amounts",
