"不平等条約 (1920 年代の中国の言葉)、領事裁判権・治外法権、協定関税、最恵国待遇、租界、カピチュレーション (オスマン)、informal empire (Gallagher & Robinson 1953)": "unequal treaties (a Chinese term of the 1920s), consular jurisdiction and extraterritoriality, conventional tariffs, most-favored-nation treatment, concessions, capitulations (Ottoman), informal empire (Gallagher & Robinson 1953)",
"法では独立国で、外交・任免・継承は自前。条約で関税を協定 (従価 5%) にされ、海関 (税関) の税務司は外国人 (ハート 1863〜1911)、外国人は領事の裁判を受け、租界は外国の行政、宣教は条約で保護された。実態は砲艦 (1856〜60 の戦争、1900 の出兵) と駐兵権 (1901 年の辛丑条約) で軍事にも入った。日本は 1894 年の日英通商航海条約で 1899 年に領事裁判権を終え、中国は 1943 年に終えた。「非公式の帝国」はラテンアメリカへの英の影響のように条約の形すらない例を指す": "De jure independent, with its own foreign affairs, appointments and succession. Treaties fixed tariffs by agreement (5% ad valorem), the Inspector General of the Maritime Customs was a foreigner (Hart 1863–1911), foreigners were tried in consular courts, the concessions were under foreign administration, and missions were protected by treaty. De facto, gunboats (the war of 1856–60, the 1900 expedition) and the right to station troops (Boxer Protocol of 1901) reached into military affairs too. Japan ended consular jurisdiction in 1899 under the Anglo-Japanese Treaty of Commerce and Navigation of 1894; China ended it in 1943. “Informal empire” refers to cases without even the form of a treaty, such as British influence in Latin America",
"南京条約 (1842 年 8 月 29 日。第 10 条 関税)、虎門寨追加条約 (1843 年 10 月 8 日。最恵国)、望厦条約 (1844 年 7 月 3 日。第 21 条 領事裁判)、天津条約 (1858 年。宣教の保護)、辛丑条約 (1901 年 9 月 7 日。駐兵)、日米修好通商条約 (1858 年 7 月 29 日。第 6 条)、日英通商航海条約 (1894 年 7 月 16 日)、中英・中米の治外法権撤廃条約 (1943 年 1 月 11 日)、ローザンヌ条約 (1923) 第 28 条、海関の統計 (Chinese Maritime Customs, Returns of Trade)": "Treaty of Nanking (August 29, 1842; Article 10: tariffs), Supplementary Treaty of the Bogue (October 8, 1843; most-favored nation), Treaty of Wanghia (July 3, 1844; Article 21: consular jurisdiction), Treaty of Tientsin (1858; protection of missions), Boxer Protocol (September 7, 1901; stationed troops), Japan–US Treaty of Amity and Commerce (July 29, 1858; Article 6), Anglo-Japanese Treaty of Commerce and Navigation (July 16, 1894), Sino-British and Sino-American treaties abolishing extraterritoriality (January 11, 1943), Treaty of Lausanne (1923), Article 28, Maritime Customs statistics (Chinese Maritime Customs, Returns of Trade)",
"Gallagher & Robinson 1953「The Imperialism of Free Trade」(EcHR 6-1) とその批判 (Platt 1968)、Kayaoğlu 2010『Legal Imperialism』(治外法権の終わり方の比較)、Wang Dong 2005『China's Unequal Treaties』、Osterhammel 1986 (半植民地の概念)。論点: 条約のない影響を「帝国」と呼べるか、半主権は型か程度か": "Gallagher & Robinson 1953, “The Imperialism of Free Trade” (EcHR 6-1) and its critique (Platt 1968); Kayaoğlu 2010, “Legal Imperialism” (comparing how extraterritoriality ended); Wang Dong 2005, “China's Unequal Treaties”; Osterhammel 1986 (the concept of semi-colonialism). Debates: can influence without treaties be called “empire”; is semi-sovereignty a type or a degree",
