"法では独立国で、条約で (1) 独立を損なう条約を他国と結ばない、(2) 米の介入権 (プラット第 3 条)、(3) 海軍基地 (第 7 条、グアンタナモ)、(4) 関税収入の管理 (ドミニカ 1907: 米の受領官が関税を集め 55% を債務に) を認める。実態は米が選挙と政権に関わり (キューバ 1906〜09 の占領、ニカラグア 1912〜33、ハイチ 1915〜34 の占領)、任免にも入った。1934 年にプラット修正は廃止され、グアンタナモだけ残った": "De jure independent, but by treaty it accepts (1) concluding no treaties with other states that impair its independence, (2) a US right of intervention (Platt, Article III), (3) naval bases (Article VII, Guantánamo), (4) control of customs revenue (Dominican Republic 1907: a US receiver collected customs and applied 55% to debt). De facto, the US had a hand in elections and governments (occupations of Cuba 1906–09, Nicaragua 1912–33, Haiti 1915–34) and reached into appointments. The Platt Amendment was abrogated in 1934; only Guantánamo remained",
"プラット修正条項 (1901 年 3 月 2 日の陸軍歳出法) と米キューバ関係条約 (1903 年 5 月 22 日。第 3・7 条)、ヘイ=ビュノー=バリヤ条約 (1903 年 11 月 18 日)、米ドミニカ協定 (1907 年 2 月 8 日)、米ハイチ条約 (1915 年 9 月 16 日)、米キューバ関係条約 (1934 年 5 月 29 日。廃止)。文書館: NARA RG 59、FRUS (米外交文書、デジタル化済み)": "Platt Amendment (Army Appropriations Act of March 2, 1901) and the US–Cuban Treaty of Relations (May 22, 1903; Articles III and VII), Hay–Bunau-Varilla Treaty (November 18, 1903), US–Dominican Convention (February 8, 1907), US–Haitian Treaty (September 16, 1915), US–Cuban Treaty of Relations (May 29, 1934; abrogation). Archives: NARA RG 59, FRUS (Foreign Relations of the United States, digitized)",
"Pérez 1986『Cuba under the Platt Amendment』、Veeser 2002『A World Safe for Capitalism』(ドミニカ)、Lake 2009 (米の上下関係の指標)。論点: 介入権は保護国か「非公式の帝国」か、財政の管理は軍事より強い従属か": "Pérez 1986, “Cuba under the Platt Amendment”; Veeser 2002, “A World Safe for Capitalism” (Dominican Republic); Lake 2009 (US hierarchy indicators). Debates: is a right of intervention a protectorate or “informal empire”; is fiscal control a stronger dependency than military control",
