"<tr><th>第 {0} の汎用技術</th><td colspan=\"3\">{1}・{2}年 — <b>{3}</b> <span class=\"muted\">(採用 {4})</span></td></tr>": "<tr><th>General-purpose technology #{0}</th><td colspan=\"3\">{1}, {2} — <b>{3}</b> <span class=\"muted\">(adoption {4})</span></td></tr>",
"<h3>{0}の研究</h3><table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>分野</th><th>技術</th><th>見えている前線</th><th>取り込める上限</th></tr>{1}<tr><th>研究者</th><td colspan=\"3\">{2} 人</td></tr>{3}</table>\n    <p class=\"note\">技術の水準は 1 人あたりの産出に掛かる。研究者の数は人口と所得と学力で決まり、分野には付加価値の比で分かれる。研究者 1 人あたりの研究の生産性は、技術が進むほど下がる (アイデアは見つけにくくなる)。予算の「教育」で学力を上げると、研究者が増えて技術も伸びる。</p>\n    <p class=\"note\">ほかの国の技術は、首都どうしの光の年数だけ遅れて伝わる (見えている前線)。学校 (就学年数と学力) が進んだ国ほど、前線の多くを取り込める (取り込める上限)。汎用技術は、採り入れはじめは補完の投資に人を回すので伸びが一度下がり (転換点)、そのあと大きく上がる (展開期)。</p>": "<h3>{0} research</h3><table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Field</th><th>Technology</th><th>Visible frontier</th><th>Absorption cap</th></tr>{1}<tr><th>Researchers</th><td colspan=\"3\">{2}</td></tr>{3}</table>\n    <p class=\"note\">The technology level multiplies output per person. The number of researchers depends on population, income and education, and they are split across fields by value-added share. Research productivity per researcher falls as technology advances (ideas get harder to find). Raising education through the “Education” budget adds researchers and speeds technology.</p>\n    <p class=\"note\">Other realms’ technology becomes visible only after the light-years between capitals (visible frontier). Realms with better schooling (years of schooling and test scores) can absorb more of the frontier (absorption cap). A general-purpose technology first lowers growth, as people are diverted to complementary investment (turning point), and then raises it sharply (deployment phase).</p>",
