"<h3>集団</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">不満の大きい集団: {0}。政治から締め出された人口 <b class=\"{1}\">{2}</b> (離反の起きやすさ ×{3})</p>\n    <details class=\"note\" data-h=\"groups\" {4}><summary>説明 — 民族と所得の分位</summary>\n      <div class=\"scroll\"><table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>民族</th><th>人口</th><th>権力への近さ</th>{5}</tr>{6}</table></div>\n      <p class=\"muted\">表の右の 5 列は、所得の分位ごとの忠誠度 (この星系の分位の所得の分け前は {7}。星系ごとの所得の偏りと土地改革から決まる。世界銀行の 2,434 国・年の中央値は {8})。締め出された集団 (無力・差別) は、権力に加わっている集団より {9} 点低い (人口で平均すると星系の忠誠度)。税は所得の多い分位ほど重く、福祉の予算は下の分位に厚い。\n      権力への近さは統治体制の実態の「統治者の任免」で決まる: 宗主が任じるなら よそ生まれが優位でここ生まれは締め出され、分け合うなら両方が加わり、従属国が任じるなら ここ生まれが優位。ほかの種族は締め出される (強制労働か「宗教と文化」を宗主が握るなら差別)。直轄の星系だけ手で変えられる。\n      締め出された人口の割合が 10 ポイント増えると、離反の起きやすさは {10} 倍 (EPR と UCDP の 159 か国 8,937 国・年。目標 R42)。</p>\n      <p class=\"muted\">価値観 (2 軸の近い形。国の平均を 0 として、国の間の差の大きさで割った値。Global Flourishing Study の 22 か国と香港の個票から): 星系の平均は 伝統 ↔ 世俗 {11} ({12})・生存 ↔ 自己表現 {13} ({14})。</p>\n      <div class=\"scroll\"><table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>価値観</th>{15}{16}</tr>\n        {17}</table></div>\n      <p class=\"muted\">世俗は宗教と法への従い方、自己表現は人の信頼・暮らしの心配のなさ・幸福から作った近い形 (世界価値観調査の 2 軸の項目の一部にあたる)。所得の上の分位ほど暮らしの心配が少なく自己表現寄り、よそ生まれは少し伝統寄り (国の中の差。民族の間の所得の差は入れていない)。</p></details>\n    {18}": "<h3>Groups</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">Most discontented group: {0}. Population excluded from politics <b class=\"{1}\">{2}</b> (secession hazard ×{3})</p>\n    <details class=\"note\" data-h=\"groups\" {4}><summary>Details — ethnicity and income quintiles</summary>\n      <div class=\"scroll\"><table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Ethnicity</th><th>Population</th><th>Access to power</th>{5}</tr>{6}</table></div>\n      <p class=\"muted\">The five right-hand columns show loyalty by income quintile (this system’s quintile income shares {7}, set by its income inequality and land reform; the median of 2,434 World Bank country-years is {8}). Excluded groups (powerless, discriminated) are {9} points lower than groups that share power (the population-weighted average is the system’s loyalty). Taxes weigh more on higher quintiles, and the welfare budget favors lower ones.\n      Access to power follows the de facto “Appointment of rulers” of the form of rule: if the suzerain appoints, those born elsewhere dominate and those born here are excluded; if shared, both take part; if the dependency appoints, those born here dominate. Other species are excluded (discriminated if there is forced labor or the suzerain holds “Religion & culture”). Only systems under direct rule can be changed by hand.\n      Each 10-point rise in the excluded share of population multiplies the secession hazard by {10} (EPR and UCDP, 159 countries, 8,937 country-years; goal R42).</p>\n      <p class=\"muted\">Values (an approximation of the two axes: the realm mean set to 0, divided by the size of differences between countries; from the individual data of the Global Flourishing Study, 22 countries plus Hong Kong): the system average is traditional ↔ secular {11} ({12}) and survival ↔ self-expression {13} ({14}).</p>\n      <div class=\"scroll\"><table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Values</th>{15}{16}</tr>\n        {17}</table></div>\n      <p class=\"muted\">Secular is approximated from religion and attitudes to law, self-expression from interpersonal trust, freedom from material worry and happiness (a subset of the items on the two World Values Survey axes). Higher income quintiles worry less about their livelihood and lean toward self-expression; those born elsewhere lean slightly traditional (within-country differences; income gaps between ethnic groups are not included).</p></details>\n    {18}",
