"<h4>入植船団 ({0}の次の入植から)</h4>\n    <p class=\"note\">入植船団は <b>{1} 隻・{2}</b> (1 隻 {3})。</p>\n    <div class=\"btns\">{4}</div>\n    {5}{6}{7}\n    <p class=\"note\">住む場所は 1 人 {8} t (1 隻 {9} 万 t)。積み荷は船団でまとめて積む。遅い船はエネルギーが少なくて済むが、着くのが遅い。</p>\n    <p class=\"note\">続く見込み (前提ごとの幅のまま): 入植地として降りてから増えていくなら <b>{10}</b>。\n      船の上で人数を保つ前提なら、HERITAGE (Marin & Beluffi 2018。定員 500 の船で 6,300 年・近親婚なし) では 98 人で足り、25 組 (50 人) では半分ほどが絶える。\n      Smith (2014。150 年・遺伝の多様性を保つ・大きな災害 1 回) では {11}〜{12}が要る ({13})。</p>": "<h4>Colony fleet (from {0}'s next colonization)</h4>\n    <p class=\"note\">The colony fleet is <b>{1} ships · {2}</b> ({3} per ship).</p>\n    <div class=\"btns\">{4}</div>\n    {5}{6}{7}\n    <p class=\"note\">Living space is {8} t per person ({9} × 10,000 t per ship). Cargo is loaded across the fleet as a whole. Slower ships need less energy but arrive later.</p>\n    <p class=\"note\">Survival outlook (ranges kept per assumption): if the colonists land and grow as a colony, <b>{10}</b>.\n      If the population must be maintained aboard: HERITAGE (Marin & Beluffi 2018; a 500-capacity ship over 6,300 years, no inbreeding) finds 98 people sufficient, while 25 couples (50 people) die out about half the time.\n      Smith (2014; 150 years, preserving genetic diversity, one major catastrophe) requires {11}–{12} ({13}).</p>",
