"<tr><td><button data-act=\"goto\" data-sys=\"{0}\">{1}</button>{2}</td><td>{3} 光年</td>\n      <td><b>{4}</b> 艦隊<br><span class=\"muted\">{5} 年前の様子</span></td><td>{6}〜{7} 艦隊</td></tr>": "<tr><td><button data-act=\"goto\" data-sys=\"{0}\">{1}</button>{2}</td><td>{3} ly</td>\n      <td><b>{4}</b> fleets<br><span class=\"muted\">As of {5} years ago</span></td><td>{6}–{7} fleets</td></tr>",
"<h3>相手が見ている{0}の艦隊</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">ほかの国の首都には、こちらの艦隊が光の遅れのぶん古い姿で見えている (こちらが把握している数は {1} 艦隊)。AI の国は、その数に読み違いを掛けて勝つ見込みを出し、宣戦や講和を決める。読み違いは相手だけが知っているので、3 回に 2 回はこの幅に入る、という幅で出す。戦争が始まると、戦って沈めた・沈められた数でも見積もりを直す。相手の首都に近い星系へ艦隊を集めると、早く見える。</p>\n    <div class=\"scroll\"><table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>国</th><th>首都までの距離</th><th>相手に見えている数</th><th>相手の見積もりの幅</th></tr>{2}</table></div>": "<h3>{0} fleets as others see them</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">Other states’ capitals see our fleets as they were, aged by the light delay (we know of {1} fleets). AI states apply a misjudgment factor to that number to estimate their chance of winning, and decide on war or peace accordingly. Only they know their misjudgment, so it is shown as a range they fall within 2 times in 3. Once a war begins, they also revise their estimate by the fleets sunk on each side. Massing fleets in systems near their capital makes them visible sooner.</p>\n    <div class=\"scroll\"><table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>State</th><th>Distance to capital</th><th>Count they see</th><th>Their estimate range</th></tr>{2}</table></div>",
