"<div class=\"kpi\">\n      <div><span>政治力</span><b>{0} / {1}</b><span>{2}{3}/年</span></div>\n      <div><span>{4}議会の支持</span><b>{5}</b><span>{6}</span></div>\n      <div><span>点数{7}</span><b>{8}</b><span>{9}</span></div>\n      <div><span>直轄</span><b>{10} / {11}</b><span>星系</span></div>\n    </div>\n    <h3>国家方針{12}</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">国の向きを一つ選ぶ。{13}年に一度だけ変えられる (政治力 {14})。議会の審議にかけ (国の権力に加わっている集団の支持が {15} 以上ならすぐ通る)、通ったあと、知らせが光速で届いた星系から順に効く。</p>\n    {16}<div class=\"btns wrap\">{17}</div>\n    {18}\n    <h3>政治力 ({19}の意志)</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">星系の政府への指令 (施設・交易路・方針・視察・要求への返事など) には政治力が要る。遠い星系ほど多く (距離 d 光年で 2 + 0.15d、直轄の星系は半分)。宣戦・講和は {20}。{21}の中の行動 ({22}からの入植船・施設) と艦隊への指令は要らない。年ごとに貯まり、{23} で頭打ちになる。</p>\n    <table class=\"tbl\">{24}<tr class=\"total\"><td>合計</td><td>{25}{26}/年</td></tr></table>\n    <h3>{27}議会の支持</h3>\n    {28}\n    <p class=\"note\">{29}の支持は毎年0.25ずつ下がる (成果を待ついら立ち)。時代の課題を果たすと +15、果たせないと −10、独立を許すと −8、独立国を降伏させると +10、{30}の入植船で新しい星系を拓くと +1。50より高ければ政治力の増え方が増え、低ければ減る (10ごとに年 ±1)。15を割ると政権交代で、国家方針が白紙に戻り、貯めた政治力を失う。</p>\n    <h3>{31}時代の課題 {32}</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">{33}年ごとに課題が2つ出る。果たすと議会の支持 +15、次の時代は果たした数 × 2 だけ政治力が年に多く増える。</p>\n    {34}\n    {35}\n    <h3>挑戦</h3>\n    {36}\n    <h3>点数{37}</h3>\n    <table class=\"tbl\">{38}<tr class=\"total\"><td>合計</td><td>{39}</td></tr></table>\n    <h3>統治体制</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">家臣の星系ごとに統治体制を選べる (星系の詳細欄の「統治」から。光速の指令)。体制によって、離反の起きやすさ・朝貢・指令の通りやすさが変わる。遠い星系ほど通信の遅れが効くので、現地に任せる体制が保ちやすい。</p>\n    <label class=\"field\">新しい入植地の統治体制<select data-act=\"regimedefault\">{40}</select></label>\n    {41}\n    <h3>直轄の星系 ({42} / {43})</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">{44}の直属の従属星系を、星系の詳細欄の「統治」から直接統治 (直轄) にできる。直轄の星系は自分では動かないので、施設や交易路は{45}が指令で決める。</p>\n    {46}": "<div class=\"kpi\">\n      <div><span>Political capital</span><b>{0} / {1}</b><span>{2}{3}/yr</span></div>\n      <div><span>{4}Council support</span><b>{5}</b><span>{6}</span></div>\n      <div><span>Score{7}</span><b>{8}</b><span>{9}</span></div>\n      <div><span>Direct rule</span><b>{10} / {11}</b><span>systems</span></div>\n    </div>\n    <h3>National policy{12}</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">Choose one course for the nation. It can be changed only once every {13} years ({14} political capital). It goes to the council for debate (it passes at once if the groups that hold power support it at {15} or more); once passed, it takes effect system by system as the news arrives at light speed.</p>\n    {16}<div class=\"btns wrap\">{17}</div>\n    {18}\n    <h3>Political capital (the will of {19})</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">Directives to system governments (facilities, trade routes, policies, inspections, answers to demands, etc.) cost political capital. Farther systems cost more (2 + 0.15d at distance d ly; half for direct-rule systems). Declaring war or making peace costs {20}. Actions within {21} (colony ships from {22}, facilities) and fleet orders cost nothing. It accrues each year and caps at {23}.</p>\n    <table class=\"tbl\">{24}<tr class=\"total\"><td>Total</td><td>{25}{26}/yr</td></tr></table>\n    <h3>{27}Council support</h3>\n    {28}\n    <p class=\"note\">{29} support falls by 0.25 each year (impatience for results). Achieving an era objective gives +15, failing one −10, allowing independence −8, forcing an independent nation to surrender +10, and opening a new system with a colony ship from {30} +1. Above 50, political capital grows faster; below 50, slower (±1/yr per 10 points). Below 15 the government falls: national policy is reset and stored political capital is lost.</p>\n    <h3>{31}Era objectives {32}</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">Two objectives are set every {33} years. Achieving one gives +15 council support, and in the next era political capital grows by 2 more per year for each one achieved.</p>\n    {34}\n    {35}\n    <h3>Challenges</h3>\n    {36}\n    <h3>Score{37}</h3>\n    <table class=\"tbl\">{38}<tr class=\"total\"><td>Total</td><td>{39}</td></tr></table>\n    <h3>Forms of rule</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">A form of rule can be chosen for each vassal system (under “Rule” in the system details; a light-speed directive). The form changes secession hazard, tribute and how readily directives are carried out. Communication delay weighs more on distant systems, so forms that leave matters to local rulers hold up better there.</p>\n    <label class=\"field\">Form of rule for new colonies<select data-act=\"regimedefault\">{40}</select></label>\n    {41}\n    <h3>Direct-rule systems ({42} / {43})</h3>\n    <p class=\"note\">Dependent systems directly under {44} can be placed under direct rule from “Rule” in the system details. Direct-rule systems do not act on their own, so {45} sets their facilities and trade routes by directive.</p>\n    {46}",
